ription":"Austria-Hungary","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-728a-bd25-c06c931b4324","description":"Bulgaria","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7683-b370-88aa047dfc55","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What Russian word describes the political and economic restructuring introduced by Soviet leader Mikhail Gorbachev in the 1980s?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Perestroika, meaning restructuring, began in 1986 alongside glasnost (openness) and contributed to the Soviet Union\'s collapse.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7ff3-8a82-b1be934a6c8c","description":"Perestroika","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7f86-afb0-e8d307150f2c","description":"Apparatchik","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7682-b7b3-368b14c19771","description":"Uskoreniye","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7021-8ecc-e645b13f3502","description":"Khozraschyot","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-73a7-b6f9-ed1916700bda","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Where did the battle of Waterloo take place?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Waterloo is in Belgium today, though the area was part of the United Kingdom of the Netherlands when the battle was fought in 1815.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7ac3-9a97-94e270f0947a","description":"Belgium","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7940-8320-67111aa6553f","description":"France","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-743e-a956-040f629bbd30","description":"England","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-72bb-9f11-3ab70801ee55","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7d01-8aeb-6105e1a21f4f","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which ancient people carved the rose-red city of Petra?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Nabataeans made Petra the center of their kingdom and engineered channels and cisterns to manage scarce water in the desert.","alternatives":[{"id":"01