":3,"explanation":"Abdullah I became Jordan\'s first king after the country gained independence in 1946.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7a96-819c-76cad89441c0","description":"Jordan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7740-b869-bd6d74e18a74","description":"Monaco","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7a27-ac65-9e97a3b1fe18","description":"Syria","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7534-a2fd-13f7a0422f24","description":"Iran","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7536-88a1-4d9b500464ae","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In 1954, which Vietnamese village was the site of the decisive battle in the Indochina War, and caused the French to be defeated?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Viet Minh victory at Dien Bien Phu in May 1954 ended French rule in Indochina.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7488-a0c6-dc540c0b9015","description":"Dien Bien Phu","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-730e-8fed-b649e8fc59ba","description":"Hue","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7b3d-9636-0e8722eacf57","description":"Saigon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-71ea-b4a5-9c0dfeaa63ac","description":"Phnom Penh","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-785f-a46c-e1b8c4dbca19","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which famous Egyptian queen married and co-ruled with her younger brother Ptolemy XIII?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Cleopatra was the last active ruler of Ptolemaic Egypt, a dynasty founded by one of Alexander the Great\u2019s generals.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7723-9b32-14bce5d699df","description":"Cleopatra","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7be5-8ab1-052099707f0b","description":"Hatshepsut","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-755c-bed4-cb3060a256b9","description":"Nefertiti","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7292-8fcf-eb48e77740fe","description":"Arsinoe IV","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64