na Capac","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7c35-b8bc-53f6bb0c56d5","description":"Pachacuti","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7ed8-963f-e15b30b43118","description":"Tupac Amaru","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7786-8bb1-b4d7011f3795","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which decade saw the Stonewall Riots in New York City, which helped to initiate the gay rights movement?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The 1960s are correct: the Stonewall uprising began on June 28, 1969, after police raided the Stonewall Inn in Greenwich Village.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-73ab-be0c-e7deb77b24ae","description":"The 1960s","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7a11-8613-4db1929ccf97","description":"The 1950s","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-73b2-8753-16e45245c3fa","description":"The 1970s","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-718e-a25f-190aac827849","description":"The 1980s","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-76c7-877d-0090e74db6a2","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which of Henry VIII\'s six wives was fourth?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Anne of Cleves remained in England after the annulment and was treated as Henry VIII\u2019s \u201cbeloved sister.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-71e1-a791-7ff59c2c1f8c","description":"Anne of Cleves","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7a9f-b410-e3cc88e113cf","description":"Anne Boleyn","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7238-8400-9a13cb2d1919","description":"Catherine Parr","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7ca6-b4b2-744a17f271f4","description":"Catherine of Aragon","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-76b7-8bb8-f4b009fe4da8","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which law professor testified at Clarence Thomas\'s 1991 Supreme Court confirmation hearings?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Anita Hill\'s testimony accused Thomas of sexu