":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"When did the United States transfer the Panama Canal to Panamanian control?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The 1977 Torrijos\u2013Carter Treaties arranged a gradual transfer, with full Panamanian control taking effect on December 31, 1999.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-73e6-9e7b-214eb86f056c","description":"1999","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7865-b4f2-6de0738da36f","description":"1987","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7d8e-b20a-32009236bf66","description":"1991","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7422-a240-68ac3aa91501","description":"1979","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-744a-928c-a0f28725b174","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"How many children did Queen Victoria have?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Queen Victoria had nine children with Prince Albert. Their descendants married into royal families across Europe, helping earn Victoria her nickname.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7551-a507-a88c574f8306","description":"Nine","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-704b-bc91-63c4f4f03ab9","description":"Five","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-795f-bbf8-debbc3c33942","description":"Seven","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7ad1-86ab-853adb172a38","description":"Twelve","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7102-ba54-cec8ee6b986b","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the first European to sight New Zealand in 1642?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Abel Tasman was a Dutch explorer, and the sea between Australia and New Zealand is named after him.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-70e9-b426-ecbd025d5d53","description":"Abel Tasman","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-773c-97fe-3a7b809d5243","description":"James Cook","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7845-85bf-e998be6285e8","description":"Christopher Columbus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"