a9e93fff2","description":"Dwight D. Eisenhower","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7bf3-8b25-d8c348ab0714","description":"Bernard Montgomery","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-77c4-a824-900c2273f1b3","description":"Erwin Rommel","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7263-99a6-1a5f83afe063","description":"Arthur Tedder","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-73cf-9d38-9eba71e8ff3a","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which German city served as the capital of West Germany from 1949 until reunification in 1990?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bonn was chosen as West Germany\u2019s provisional capital. After reunification, parliament voted to move the seat of government to Berlin, a transfer completed in 1999.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7d08-ba6c-545b14787a7d","description":"Bonn","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-77da-9290-86f92cecfa2e","description":"Munich","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7e46-816e-6b2139ab8014","description":"Berlin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-736b-b04d-928b66e9a36d","description":"Frankfurt","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-73d4-af27-65bb6a6c6a12","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the name of the Viking settlement that was established in Newfoundland, Canada?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"L\'Anse aux Meadows contains remains of Norse-style buildings, evidence of a European presence in North America centuries before Columbus.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-75ce-9d4f-a3007baa8867","description":"L\'Anse aux Meadows","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7369-a2cf-b87f4f324e69","description":"Quebec","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-732c-a760-921c7ca91fbc","description":"Hedgesville","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7478-9f01-df397faab734","description":"Iceland","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7cdf-9b3e-8509065d679d","category":"01a21312