riefly known as the Batavian Republic?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Netherlands\' Batavian Republic was a French-backed successor to the Dutch Republic; in 1806, Napoleon replaced it with the Kingdom of Holland.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-74b0-8f49-842c64b524fc","description":"The Netherlands","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-70e2-89ae-fdb29f67359d","description":"Poland","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-70c8-b3d8-4196c08be508","description":"Portugal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7c13-9f40-fbc8d1b9585d","description":"Greece","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-70ea-83aa-4533f95b3615","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the Gulf War begin?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Gulf War began in 1990 after Iraq invaded Kuwait; the U.S.-led coalition launched Operation Desert Storm the following January.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-75ad-961c-f7fa40a4dbfd","description":"1990","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7f66-9b2a-0c13ccece251","description":"1983","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7df5-be90-cb3a9ea6897c","description":"1971","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7522-b869-3af86d0fc04d","description":"1999","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7aa6-aea9-5eef58497be4","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"The Battle of Rorke\'s Drift in 1879 featured in which war?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Zulu War was fought between the British Empire and the Zulu Kingdom. Rorke\'s Drift was one of its best-known engagements.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-74b4-811c-12c35d6d156c","description":"Zulu War","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-76c2-811a-5d7b66d12c16","description":"Vietnam War","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7ff0-a018-47574463a207","description":"Spanish Civil War","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7cf6-bd7e-8e4114e5d146","description":"Russian Civil War","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7014-ac47-77117ce74bd5","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was born in Assisi in 1181 and later became a missionary?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"St. Francis founded the Order of Friars Minor, whose members are commonly called Franciscans.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7f96-b388-3edb67564522","description":"St. Francis","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-78d7-b461-fd6a156ccc67","description":"St. Peter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7476-bd55-f6081ad7778a","description":"St. Paul","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7ca4-baf4-4412f8a98adc","description":"St. Augustine","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-78ae-b720-2723a3604651","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the Boeing 747 enter regular passenger service?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Boeing 747 entered regular passenger service in 1970, with Pan Am\'s inaugural commercial flight from New York to London.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-77fe-892e-46fb247472f5","description":"1970","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7708-878f-5efde4b759d9","description":"1966","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7ff1-89fa-c48211d94771","description":"1974","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7440-92ab-3166dad471c2","description":"1978","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-77cd-9c28-d3d7f9394d10","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In 1956, Tunisia gained independence from which country?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Independence ended the French protectorate established in 1881; Habib Bourguiba became Tunisia\u2019s first president.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-70ae-949d-d03cba0e9afe","description":"France","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-73e8-b076-e165c6b05c93","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7e10-847b-2c0b552057