00-8440-f3d8ad962e53","description":"Britain and Zanzibar","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-759f-810b-2af2341b4408","description":"France and Mauritania","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7be6-a337-abcf8b351a9c","description":"Belgium and The Netherlands","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-76e4-9d90-1f834598b9f8","description":"India and Fiji","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7dc2-85d9-7ea83315c82f","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was British Prime Minister when King Edward VIII abdicated in 1936?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The crisis arose from Edward\'s wish to marry Wallis Simpson; Baldwin\'s government would not accept her as queen, and Edward chose to abdicate.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-71c2-b8a2-54fb35c2b874","description":"Stanley Baldwin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-74b0-b7d0-445bbd132be9","description":"Anthony Eden","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7b87-afcf-431fb4c2fad7","description":"Winston Churchill","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7622-b0a2-eb91c595cc29","description":"Neville Chamberlain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7eb8-a3a9-5e5987d8a7b2","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which English king reputedly lost his crown jewels while crossing the Wash?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"King John\u2019s baggage train was said to have been swept away by the Wash\u2019s tides, though whether the crown jewels were truly lost remains uncertain.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-76d8-a283-b13c087b0eda","description":"King John","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7e71-afcf-bf5a57f1a59a","description":"Richard I","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7116-9cc4-c4bda9549a6b","description":"Henry III","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-795e-9582-347bac47c5d8","description":"Edward II","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7bb9-9728-dcf8e4352238","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which city was burned by General Sherman in 1864?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Atlanta was an important Confederate rail and supply center. Sherman\u2019s forces captured it in September 1864 and burned much of the city before beginning the March to the Sea.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7105-8dd6-f9ffaf7e5329","description":"Atlanta","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-765e-8171-bbf625a1855c","description":"Dallas","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7fe3-9319-c746267baeb4","description":"Houston","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-76af-9e98-c039928c08a4","description":"Columbus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-764b-9db8-55a58ad1aa8a","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the 30th president of the USA, in term during the period 1923\u20131929?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Calvin Coolidge was nicknamed \u201cSilent Cal\u201d for his reserved manner and is associated with the phrase \u201cThe business of America is business.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-73b7-b6f2-a6005ca81f45","description":"Calvin Coolidge","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7790-879a-9f61460fdcfb","description":"Martin Van Buren","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-74e4-be67-2380b8fc2788","description":"Grover Cleveland","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7081-bef3-0f1953d75743","description":"Rutherford B. Hayes","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae64-7ed7-9259-2a79424749aa","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In 1900, a sealed library cave holding tens of thousands of ancient manuscripts was found in which Buddhist cave complex in China\'s Gobi region?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The cache is often called the Dunhuang Library Cave. Its manuscripts include Buddhist scriptures as well as secular documents, and many are now held in institutions around the world.","alternatives"