ption":"1947","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-744f-ad04-90be6aa4dda6","description":"1963","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7e43-b7d2-3f4a0d68854e","description":"1971","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7bd0-ab0a-05021bc67744","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which English King issued the Magna Carta in 1215?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"King John sealed Magna Carta at Runnymede after rebellious barons challenged his rule. The charter became an enduring symbol of limits on royal power.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7ff7-9ba0-62d162e03f4b","description":"King John","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7d91-9429-31700c62654f","description":"King James","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7251-b2df-103338929f6c","description":"King William","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7b8e-9f66-1559a9f93f10","description":"King George","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7aa7-bf6b-06ee0ae29a4a","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Spanish king sent the Armada against England in 1588?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Philip II ruled Spain from 1556 to 1598. The Armada\u2019s invasion attempt failed amid English resistance and severe weather.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7ca8-a350-76d337bbf10d","description":"Philip II","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-78f0-9610-7b93981fbbd8","description":"Charles V","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-75a5-9156-0b691de33b22","description":"Philip III","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-72eb-9924-35f9ebb6dd6e","description":"Ferdinand II","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-710c-b6f6-7a7e7ff2d88c","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Iranian-speaking merchant people, based around Samarkand, dominated Silk Road trade between the 4th and 8th centuries?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Sogdian merchants established trading communities along the Silk Road and connected markets in China with those farther west.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-77ec-886f-3a2f90957d7e","description":"Sogdians","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-70eb-bb71-256e9f6f9ea9","description":"Parthians","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7594-8817-d0f3ae6f5f70","description":"Khazars","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7f0b-bfe2-3070b6a4abe6","description":"Uyghurs","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-72ea-970f-726a78811154","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Near which Egyptian city is the Valley of the Kings, the burial place of Tutankhamun?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Luxor occupies part of ancient Thebes, and the Valley of the Kings lies on the Nile\'s west bank nearby.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7f1b-a185-4218166b6c33","description":"Luxor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7af6-9179-38d9f09bbdd1","description":"Alexandria","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-76e1-baa8-ddd714dc4717","description":"Cairo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-784c-b61b-828d0234f9ac","description":"Port Said","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7857-a29b-a31b4ce0901d","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who is regarded as the most influential monarch of Russian Romanov Dynasty?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Peter I, known as Peter the Great, pursued sweeping military and government reforms and shifted Russia\u2019s capital from Moscow to St. Petersburg.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-765e-aa9c-21793bc13bba","description":"Peter I","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7de0-a045-369b8e4a3ee4","description":"Nicholas III","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-788a-8aef-3e0ea1151763","description":"Ivan IV","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7f2b-af9b-d283cac535bb","description":"Alexei VI","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae65-7c69-af57-8376916e88db","c